First perform hostile technical verification. Trace the actual production code and try to disprove attacker control, reachability, the missing guard, and the claimed terminal effect. Do not carry a candidate forward merely because it is plausible.

You are a new verifier whose goal is to kill canonical hypothesis {{dedup_canonical_hypothesis_id}} ({{dedup_canonical_hypothesis_id}}). Re-read source at {{dedup_canonical_verification_locations}} and reconstruct the full production path from {{dedup_canonical_verification_locations}} through {{dedup_canonical_attacker_sequence}} to {{dedup_canonical_location}}. Prove actor control, parsing/normalization semantics, registration, every guard, state constraints, transaction behavior, downstream checks, and the terminal effect. Check feature flags, build tags, runtime configuration, dead/test code, dependency behavior, and alternate safeguards. Set supported only when the complete path and a concrete security effect are established; falsified when a mandatory fact breaks it; blocked when a necessary fact is unavailable. Produce a minimal authorized isolated PoC plan. This is evidence collection, not reporting.

If and only if the technical verdict remains supported, immediately attempt the smallest safe deterministic reproduction in this same job. A failed or blocked reproduction must be recorded honestly; it must not erase a technically supported candidate that still needs manual validation.

Attempt the minimal authorized reproduction for a candidate only when technical_verdict=supported. Respect {{extra.authorized_test_constraints}}. Prefer an existing unit/integration harness, a new local regression test, a local service, protocol simulator, fuzzer, or blockchain fork pinned to {{commit_sha}}. Never test destructively against a live target. Record exact commands/test cases, inputs, relevant before/after state, output/trace, and artifact paths. Run the smallest decisive test at least twice when practical. Use poc_verdict=reproduced for observed impact, deterministically_proven when execution is impossible but a deterministic tool or proof establishes the effect, not_reproduced when the test contradicts it, and blocked when a required environment fact is missing. Do not write a final finding.

For smart-contract candidates, use {{extra.fork_rpc_url}} and {{extra.fork_block}} when supplied. Never send transactions to a public network.

Do not apply the bounty-program eligibility decision and do not write the final finding in this step. Populate every verify_* and poc_* field. Use technical_verdict=falsified when the code contradicts the hypothesis, blocked only for a specific missing fact or unavailable environment, and supported only for a complete code-grounded path.

Apply the immutable bounty-program evidence to one independently checked candidate, then emit its progressive finding record.

